# Template for .leak-check-local-patterns — copy it to that name (no
# ".example") and add your own entries.
#
# The real file holds site-specific strings the generic patterns in
# scripts/leak-check.conf cannot know: your hostnames, usernames, domain
# names, machine names and similar.
#
# Format:
#   - One pattern per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#   - Each pattern is a fixed string, not a regex; characters such as . and *
#     match themselves.
#   - Matching is case-insensitive.
#
# The real file is never committed: it is listed in .gitignore. If it is
# absent, the leak check skips only this local-patterns part and still runs
# every generic pattern.
#
# This template holds no real identifiers. Replace the placeholders below.
#
# my-workstation
# my-build-server.internal
# example-username
